 "uncertainty": "FK integrity is preserved: nullable FKs (donations.projectid, resources.projectid, essays.projectid) receive NULL values only, never orphan values, so declared foreign key constraints hold. Parent rows without children are obtained by leaving some projects unreferenced. essays.projectid must be drawn from the projects.projectid pool so essays.teacher_acctid can be copied from the matching project (non-orphan rows get non-NULL teacher_acctid; NULL only where the parent teacher_acctid is NULL). donation_total formula holds only when optional support is included; conditional variant covers the other case. Derived formulas are asserted only for non-NULL operands (SQL three-valued logic); planted NULLs are never replaced. Some enum pools (payment_method, resource_type) may have additional values not shown in the sample. school_metro NULL share 12.2% observed."
